uni-meter Gentoo overlay notes
==============================

Installed paths:
- application: /opt/uni-meter
- main config: /etc/uni-meter.conf
- logback config: /etc/uni-meter/logback.xml
- service wrapper: /usr/libexec/uni-meter-run

Basic install:
  ebuild /var/db/repos/<overlay>/acct-group/uni-meter/uni-meter-0.ebuild manifest
  ebuild /var/db/repos/<overlay>/acct-user/uni-meter/uni-meter-0.ebuild manifest
  ebuild /var/db/repos/<overlay>/app-misc/uni-meter/uni-meter-1.4.1.ebuild manifest
  emerge -av acct-group/uni-meter acct-user/uni-meter app-misc/uni-meter

Enable services:
  rc-update add avahi-daemon default
  rc-update add uni-meter default

Notes:
- The example config uses Home Assistant as input and Shelly Pro 3EM as output.
- Adjust the Home Assistant URL, token, IPs, and MAC before starting.
- The example uses port 8080 for the Shelly Pro 3EM emulation and 8081 for uni-meter's own HTTP server.
